        {
            "_id": "glofNcdFzmm2AjaU",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp",
            "name": "Confident Ramble",
            "sort": 1100000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "passive"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": null
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>A puntzelken's unwavering certainty is so strong that they sway the minds of others. The puntzelken spends 1 minute expounding on a topic related to one of their Lore skills, making obviously wrong claims. Any creature that pays attention or engages them in conversation must attempt a @Check[will|dc:22] save. Regardless of the outcome, the creature is temporarily immune to Confident Rambles for 1 hour.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unconvinced and gains a +1 circumstance bonus to its saves and DCs against the puntzelken's Deception, Diplomacy, and Intimidation skill actions for 1 hour.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unconvinced.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature believes the puntzelken's claims for 1 minute. It can attempt a new saving throw if presented with clear evidence against the puntzelken's claims but can't attempt more than one save per piece of evidence. Failed saving throws don't extend the effect's duration.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the duration is 1 hour.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
